    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nI hope this is not a silly request. I was hoping I could have `mini.animate` work out of the box like I did with other plugins in AstroNvim but it just doesn't work. As in, nothing happening (apart from the plugin being installed correctly).\r\n\r\nDo you know if I'm doing something wrong?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.4\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThis is the relevant portion in my `init.lua`:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsetup.mini = require(user_path..\"plugins.mini\")\r\n...\r\nreturn {\r\n   options = setup.options,\r\n   mappings = setup.mappings,\r\n   colorscheme = setup.colorscheme,\r\n   plugins = {\r\n...\r\n      {\r\n         'echasnovski/mini.nvim',\r\n         config = setup.mini,\r\n      },\r\n...\r\n   },\r\n...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd this is the `plugins/mini.lua`:\r\n\r\n```\r\nreturn function()\r\n  require('mini.animate').setup{}\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is the same I used for other plugins such as `colorizer.nvim` and `alpha.nvim`, but just nothing happens after it completes installing `mini`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSomething.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNothing.",
