            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am not familiar with how AstroNvim works. Two basic steps that are enough to make 'mini.animate' work are:\r\n- Install 'mini.nvim' (or 'mini.animate' separately). That is, download its source code in the appropriate location and make Neovim now about it. Usually plugin manager takes care of this.\r\n- Call `require('mini.animate').setup()`. Either inside config file during startup or manually after Neovim is opened.\r\n\r\nMy first step towards solving this would be to ensure that `require('mini.animate').setup()` was properly called. This can be done checking in two places:\r\n- Execute `:=type(MiniAnimate)`. If it prints `table`, then OK; anything else - not OK.\r\n- Execute `:au MiniAnimate`. It should print several lines (like containing `MiniAnimate WinScrolled`) indicating that autocommands are set up correctly.\r\n\r\nI'll close this as out of scope with an advice to try and ask somewhere with a more concentration of knowledge about AstroNvim than here.",
